    "result_text": "The project's test suite consists of the acceptance tests, and the full `mvn test` build succeeds.\n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe acceptance tests (`AcceptanceTest`) POST to `/api/owners` and read back `$.contactPreference` from `GET /api/owners/{id}`. The response body is an `OwnerDto`, generated from the OpenAPI spec and populated from the `Owner` entity by MapStruct (which maps derived getters like `getMembershipLevel`/`getLocality` to matching DTO fields by name).\n\nFollowing that existing pattern, I added `contactPreference` in two places:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 a derived getter:\n   ```java\n   public String getContactPreference() {\n       return (this.email != null && !this.email.isEmpty()) ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";\n   }\n   ```\n   This mirrors the existing \"email is present\" test used by `getMembershipLevel` (non-null and non-empty).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 a `readOnly` `contactPreference: string` property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it from the getter by name.\n\n**Results:** Both new tests pass (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`), and `./mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
